# REST API STANDARDS

## 1. Uniform Response Format
All JSON responses must follow this structure:
- On success: `{"status": "success", "data": ...}`
- On error: `{"status": "error", "message": "Human-readable description", "code": 400}`

## 2. HTTP Status Codes and Validation
- `200 OK` : Successful read or update.
- `201 Created` : Resource created.
- `400 Bad Request` : Invalid input data (include validation details).
- `401 / 403` : Missing authentication / Forbidden access.
- `404 Not Found` : Resource not found.
- `500 Internal Error` : Server error (never expose internal error details to the client).

## 3. Required Endpoints
- Always include a `GET /healthz` endpoint to check server status.
